    "durationMs": 360247,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Here's a summary of what I built:\n\n**Implementation** (ASP.NET Core 8.0, C# 12, EF Core + Npgsql):\n- `Program.cs` — minimal API with `POST /links`, `GET /links`, `GET /links/{code}`, `GET /r/{code}`, plus a `migrate` CLI command. JSON bodies are parsed manually so malformed JSON, missing/invalid `url`, and invalid `code` all return 422 with an `error` field; duplicates return 409; unknown codes return 404. Redirects use an atomic SQL `clicks = clicks + 1` (EF `ExecuteUpdateAsync`) so concurrent clicks each count exactly once. URLs are stored and echoed unchanged.\n- `LinkRules.cs` — code validation (`^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`), absolute http/https URL validation, and crypto-random generated codes (8 chars, collision-checked).\n- `DbUrl.cs` — parses `DATABASE_URL` (userinfo, host, port, database, query params) into an Npgsql connection string; nothing hard-coded.\n- `Data/AppDbContext.cs` + `Models/Link.cs` + committed EF `Migrations/` (unique index on code, identity ordering).\n\n**Operations**: `sh start.sh` rebuilds only if the Release binary is missing, applies pending migrations via the app's `migrate` command, then `exec`s the server in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`. Dependencies (NuGet, dotnet-ef) were installed during development; the migration runs idempotently against `__EFMigrationsHistory`. README includes a \"Running the server\" section.\n\n**Verification**: a 41-check curl battery passed clean — create/echo/clicks=0, custom codes, boundary lengths (4 and 20), 409 duplicates, seven invalid-URL shapes, six invalid-code shapes, malformed/truncated/array bodies → 422, 302 with exact `Location`, unknown-code 404s, 10 concurrent redirects counting correctly, and ascending list order with matching `total`. I also confirmed data and click counts survive a full server restart, a cold rebuild from no `bin`/`obj` works, and left the database pristine (table truncated, migrations applied) with port 8000 free."
  }
